      {
       "data": "Out[42]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{(S,P)} & \\text{mu} & \\text{k} & \\text{O q\\_k\\^{}[2]} & \\text{Odag q\\^{}k} & \\text{deg q\\^{}k} & \\text{mu\\_k}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,1,1,0\\right\\} & 1 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,1,1,0\\right\\} & 2 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,1,1,0\\right\\} & 3 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,1,1,0\\right\\} & 4 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,3,1,0\\right\\} & 1 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 4\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,3,1,0\\right\\} & 2 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,3,1,0\\right\\} & 3 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,3,1,0\\right\\} & 4 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "73b942df-8644-4a91-b6cc-cfeba5118b43"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. The measure and the scalar product\n\nThe SoV measure is the ratio of rotated Gamma functions, $\\Gamma[F(u+h)]/\\Gamma[F(u)] = F(u)$, which telescopes per site:\n\n$$\\mu(u) = \\frac{\\Gamma[\\nu_1^{[2]}(u)]}{\\Gamma[\\nu_4^{[2]}(u)]} = \\prod_{\\alpha=1}^{2}\\prod_{n=0}^{S_\\alpha-1}\\frac{1}{u-\\theta_\\alpha-nh}\\ ,\\qquad S_1 = S,\\ S_2 = P\\ .$$\n\nAfter the alignment of the derivation (see the `.tex`) every term of the orthogonality identity carries the **same** effective measure,\n\n$$E_1(u) = \\frac{\\mu(u)}{\\nu_1(u)} = \\prod_{\\alpha}\\prod_{n=0}^{S_\\alpha}\\frac{1}{u-\\theta_\\alpha-nh}\\ ,$$\n\nwhose poles are two contiguous ladders, $S_\\alpha+1$ rungs per site. The scalar-product matrix is\n\n$$\\mathcal M^{AB}_{(\\alpha,i,j),\\,(r,\\beta)} \\;=\\; \\oint_{\\mathcal C} du\\ E_1(u)\\ e^{2\\pi i u (\\alpha-1)/h}\\ u^{\\beta}\\ \\big[\\hat q^{\\,j}_A\\,\\hat q^{\\,B}_i\\big]_r(u)\\ ,$$\n\nthe contour encircling **all** poles, with\n\n| rows $(\\alpha,i,j)$ | columns $(r,\\beta)$ |\n|---|---|\n| $\\alpha=1,2$: $\\alpha=2$ inserts the $h$-periodic $e^{2\\pi i u/h}$ | $r=1:\\ \\hat q^{\\,j}_A(u)\\,\\hat q^{\\,B}_i(u)$ |\n| $i \\in \\{1,2\\}$ | $r=21:\\ \\hat q^{\\,j}_A(u)\\,\\hat q^{\\,B}_i(u-h)$ |\n| $j \\in \\{3,4\\}$ | $r=22:\\ \\hat q^{\\,j}_A(u+h)\\,\\hat q^{\\,B}_i(u)$ |\n| | $r=3:\\ \\hat q^{\\,j}_A(u+h)\\,\\hat q^{\\,B}_i(u-h)$, and $\\beta = 0,1$ |\n\n$8\\times8$. The periodic factor is admissible exactly because $e^{2\\pi i(u+h)/h} = e^{2\\pi i u/h}$: it is inert under every shift used in the alignment, so it supplies a second independent functional on the same ladder.\n\n**Orthogonality.** The eight differences of integrals of motion between $A$ and $B$ form a kernel vector of $\\mathcal M^{AB}$, nonzero exactly when $A \\neq B$:\n\n$$\\det\\mathcal M^{AB} = 0 \\quad (A\\neq B)\\ ,\\qquad \\det\\mathcal M^{AA} \\neq 0\\ .$$",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 4. Measure, contour, and the 8x8 scalar-product matrix -------------------------------- *)\nClearAll[mPoles, mMeas, E1meas, ladE1, perFac, brkE1, spMatFSoV];\n\n(* the Gamma-ratio measure: S_alpha simple poles per site at theta_alpha + n h *)\nmPoles[SSa_, tha_, sub_] := Table[(tha /. sub) + n (h /. sub), {n, 0, SSa - 1}];\nmMeas[SS_, PP_, sub_][x_] := 1/Product[x - p, {p, Join[mPoles[SS, θ1, sub], mPoles[PP, θ2, sub]]}];\n\n(* the common effective measure E1 = mu/nu1, and its pole ladder *)\nE1meas[SS_, PP_, sub_][y_] := (mMeas[SS, PP, sub][y]/ν1[SS, PP][y]) /. sub;\nladE1[SS_, PP_, sub_] := Join[Table[(θ1 /. sub) + n (h /. sub), {n, 0, SS}], Table[(θ2 /. sub) + n (h /. sub), {n, 0, PP}]];\n\n(* alpha = 2 inserts the h-periodic function *)\nperFac[al_, sub_][x_] := If[al == 1, 1, Exp[2 Pi I x/(h /. sub)]];\nbrkE1[SS_, PP_, sub_][f_, al_, x_] := Total[Table[Residue[(E1meas[SS, PP, sub][x] perFac[al, sub][x] f), {x, p}], {p, ladE1[SS, PP, sub]}]];\n\nspMatFSoV[SS_, PP_, rA_, rB_, sub_] := Module[{x, hh = h /. sub, rows, cols, pair},\n  rows = Flatten[Table[{al, i, j}, {al, 2}, {i, {1, 2}}, {j, {3, 4}}], 2];\n  cols = Flatten[Table[{r, be}, {r, {1, 21, 22, 3}}, {be, {0, 1}}], 1];\n  pair[i_, j_, r_, y_] := Module[{qa = qdualhat[SS, PP, rA, sub][j], qb = qhat[rB, sub][i]},\n     Switch[r, 1, qa[y] qb[y], 21, qa[y] qb[y - hh], 22, qa[y + hh] qb[y], 3, qa[y + hh] qb[y - hh]]];\n  Outer[brkE1[SS, PP, sub][x^#2[[2]] pair[#1[[2]], #1[[3]], #2[[1]], x], #1[[1]], x] &, rows, cols, 1]];\n\n\"4. scalar product loaded\"",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"961317\" data-output-id=\"95\" data-out-n=\"51\" data-sub-idx=\"12\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"7\" data-sub-start=\"22\" data-sub-end=\"22\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[51]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"28\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7NC4gc2NhbGFyIHByb2R1Y3QgbG9hZGVkfQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">4. scalar product loaded</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[51]= \\text{4. scalar product loaded}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "e3ec1478-edfd-4aca-ab2b-deaa1b09f553"
    }
